00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:05.160
I'm taking a trip to eternity
eien no tabi wo shiteru

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:19.370
I continued the search on the cold tip of the finger
tsumetai yubisaki sagashi tsuzuketeta

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:24.740
It's burning from the fragments
kakera kara yaiteru

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:31.200
Hugging deep in my heart
tsuyoku mune ni dakishimete

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:38.280
The lost item that I was searching for
sagashiteita nakushimono

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.750
Checking for it in both of my hands
ryoute no naka tashikamete

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:57.130
The time that meets the new morning
atarashii asa ni deau toki ga ugakidasuyo

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:10.630
To Night

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:30.170
Welcome back.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:32.110
What happened?

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:37.440
I fell down.

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:40.610
I couldn't clear the fence when I tried to jump it.

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:43.610
Welcome back.

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:45.070
Wasn't it cold out there?

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:46.810
The bath is ready.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:47.650
Sure!

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:18.730
It wasn't... a dream...

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:30.400
An incident far from reality...

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:33.060
An invisible monster...

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:37.070
A girl who fights with only a sword...

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:44.510
I am... one who defeats monsters...

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:52.160
I don't know... What the hell is going on here?

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.160
What happened?

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:21.530
At a time like this.

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:25.570
What the...?

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:29.980
Au... Auuu... You surprised me.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.800
What is that?

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.660
It looks like konnyaku to me.
(TL Note: Konnyaku is a gelatinous food made from devil's-tongue starch.)

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.420
(TL Note: Konnyaku is a gelatinous food made from devil's-tongue starch.)

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:47.450
What were you going to do with that?
(TL Note: Konnyaku is a gelatinous food made from devil's-tongue starch.)

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:50.650
What were you going to do with that?

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.330
T-This is...

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:58.050
I was hungry so...

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:03.410
So why the hell do I have to eat konnyaku with you this late at night?

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:05.650
Auuu...

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:09.220
I'm sorry.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.170
Was dinner not enough?

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:15.670
Since you're at a growing age,

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:22.320
I guess I need to make the portions larger.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:25.370
I-I don't think Akiko-san should be blamed.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.050
Please wait.

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:31.260
I'll make a midnight snack.

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:33.840
It's alright!

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:35.420
I'm not hungry!

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:35.640
I said I'm not hungry!

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:36.900
You should take other people's goodwill into consideration.
I said I'm not hungry!

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:38.080
You should take other people's goodwill into consideration.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:39.450
See ya!

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:42.600
Auuuu...

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:48.630
Geez, she's such a nuisance.

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:08.880
What's wrong? You don't look well.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:10.590
It's heartburn.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:13.870
But you're the one who begged for a midnight snack.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:15.890
I wasn't begging.

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:17.380
That was because Yuuichi...

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.310
"Me"? What?

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.430
Remember.

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:41.220
What's wrong?

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:42.340
Nothing.

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:44.920
You've been acting strange since last night, Yuuichi...

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:46.490
You think so...?

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:49.300
Good morning.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:51.570
What happened? Did you cut yourself while shaving?

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:52.890
No... Uh...

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.680
Hey, have you heard any weird rumors about this school?

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:57.880
Weird rumors?

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:03.350
For example, a monster appearing every night, or a girl who walks into the school yard holding a sword.

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:05.350
I have.

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:06.470
Really!?

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:10.530
"Hanako-san of the toilet",  "The cursed piano" or "A human body model moving during the night".
(TL Note: These are some of the "7 school mysteries" that attempt to explain curses or strange occurrences at school. The most famous is "Hanako-san of the toilet".  Check out Haunted Junction for an anime that focuses on these "7 school mysteries")

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:13.230
No, not like that.

00:07:13.670 --> 00:07:15.670
Don't be silly in the morning.

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:17.740
It's a true story.

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:20.240
Last night, I'm sure that...

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:27.780
Hey, Aizawa!

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:29.520
Good morning.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.260
Thanks a lot last night.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:35.750
Uh, don't you remember me?

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:39.820
Hey, wait a sec!

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:40.740
Mai!

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:49.440
Do you know her?

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:53.200
That's Kawasumi Mai from 3rd year.

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:55.440
You shouldn't go near her.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:57.430
What do you mean by that?

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:59.030
You'll understand someday.

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:18.500
We got a late start.

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:22.120
If we drive them out, maybe a table will open up.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.120
Don't drive them out!

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:26.880
Oh! Over there is free!

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:30.730
May we sit here?

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:33.620
What do you want?

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:36.170
"What"? I was thinking about sharing the table...

00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:36.510
Idiot! Stop it!
"What"? I was thinking about sharing the table...

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:37.120
Idiot! Stop it!

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:38.050
S... Sorry!

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:38.750
He's a transfer student so...
S... Sorry!

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:40.150
He's a transfer student so...

00:08:40.210 --> 00:08:42.170
Hey, what are you trying to do to me?

00:08:42.170 --> 00:08:42.840
Idiot!

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:45.030
That's the school council president, Kuze!

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.250
If he starts to notice you, it will be scary later on!

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:49.160
Huh? Why?

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:51.340
He's the son of a local land owner.

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:53.360
He has quite a bit of influence around here.

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:54.990
So everybody does favors for him all the time.

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:57.430
Are there such things like that in these times?

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:59.000
I don't want to approve of it.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:01.640
It's a wild dog! There's a wild dog roaming the school yard!

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:11.510
This place is entirely different from where I was living before.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:23.520
Shiori!

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:33.620
Yuuichi!

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.050
Shiori!

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:37.120
Yuuichi-san!

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:41.410
Nayuki! Take her and run!

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:42.870
B-But...

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:44.160
It's okay! Hurry!

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:47.440
Hurry.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.180
Hey, over here!

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:56.220
Shiori!

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:12.580
Hey you! Are you alright?

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:13.810
Y-Yeah...

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:17.200
We contacted the public heath center, so I think it'll be alright now.

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:21.470
Wait Kawasumi! Where are you trying to go!?

00:10:23.570 --> 00:10:26.120
I'm telling you, what do you plan to do when there's an injury!?

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:29.570
She saved us! How can you say that to her!?

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:30.950
You be quiet.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:34.680
Geez, you always create problems all the time...

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:35.890
Ah! Hey, wait!!!

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:38.160
I'm not done talking! Hey!

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:39.390
Kawasumi!

00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:40.510
Yuuichi-san...

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:42.250
Go home through the back gate.

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:45.310
It won't be good if you are questioned.

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:47.020
Yes... Um...

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:48.840
Thank you very much.

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:54.370
Yuuichi, do you know that girl?

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:55.320
Yeah...

00:10:55.970 --> 00:10:58.070
Sorry, start your lunch without me.

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:00.600
Aizawa-kun!

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:25.420
You were right here.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:31.450
Hey wait! Let me thank you.

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:33.780
Thanks. I was saved.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.920
It's the second time... that you saved me.

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:43.320
Aren't you scared?

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:47.240
Compared to the monster from last night, that was nothing.

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:49.990
It was just hungry.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:54.540
It was just hungry and nervous.

00:11:55.100 --> 00:12:01.070
That dog came to school like that before to find food.

00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:02.000
You are...?

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:03.880
I'm Kurata Sayuri.

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:06.070
Are you Mai's acquaintance?

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:07.410
Not at all.

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:08.840
Oh.

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:10.360
"Not at all."

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:14.540
Well let's just say I met her last night.

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:18.160
And you both fell in love then?

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:20.430
I don't know about that.

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:23.150
You're right.

00:12:24.020 --> 00:12:26.120
Hey Mai, introduce yourself.

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:28.840
Kawasumi Mai...

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:30.780
I'm Aizawa Yuuichi.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:31.870
Aizawa-san?

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:33.500
Just "Aizawa".

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:36.140
Because you are my senior, it's fine to call me without "san".

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:37.870
Yeah, you're right.

00:12:42.390 --> 00:12:44.800
Yuuichi-san, did you have lunch yet?

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:47.640
If it's alright, how about eating with us?

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:49.850
Um, but I...

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:02.560
I don't mind eating, but why out here?

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:08.030
I think it's better to eat lunch like this than on a desk.

00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:12.520
Does that mean... You always eat like this?

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:15.770
Yep. We always have a bento,

00:13:15.880 --> 00:13:17.770
but we just gave it to the dog.

00:13:18.010 --> 00:13:19.750
How wasteful.

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:22.590
If you were going to give it to the dog, I would have eaten it instead.

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:26.850
Then starting tomorrow, I'll make some for Yuuichi-san too.

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:29.510
U-Um, I think that'd be awkward.

00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:31.000
It's alright.

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:34.140
My bento is highly recommended.

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:35.290
Right, Mai?

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:40.310
Was she like that before?

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:43.060
She was like that when I first met her.

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:43.960
Always?

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:47.130
Yeah, she was like that when I first met her when we started school.

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:51.510
You are really good friends with her.

00:13:52.210 --> 00:13:54.960
Yuuichi-san is already her friend too.

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:06.010
After all that, I couldn't ask about last night's incident...

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:09.930
I am... one who defeats monsters...

00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:12.770
Even so, does Sayuri-san know?

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:14.340
About that monster...

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:15.490
Yuuichi-kun!

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:19.720
Ughuu...

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:21.600
Are you alright?

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:24.490
I'm not alright!

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:27.160
I felt a gloomy aura so unexpectedly.

00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:29.010
I don't have a gloomy aura.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:31.030
Ayu, why don't you learn judo?

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:32.800
You can learn the ukemi.
(TL Note: Ukemi is a defensive fall in Judo.)

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:32.880
(TL Note: Ukemi is a defensive fall in Judo.)

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:34.420
I don't want to learn it!
(TL Note: Ukemi is a defensive fall in Judo.)

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:36.810
You're always around here.

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:38.490
Do you have a lot of free time?

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:40.090
It's not free time.

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:43.170
I'm searching for my lost article.

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:45.890
That reminds me, she said something like that before...

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:48.190
You still can't find it?

00:14:48.390 --> 00:14:50.070
Ughuu...

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:51.140
Should I help you?

00:14:52.090 --> 00:14:53.050
Really?

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:55.850
I was just grumbling then so...

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:57.000
Let's go, Yuuichi-kun!

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:57.310
Hey wait a sec! Hey!
Let's go, Yuuichi-kun!

00:14:57.310 --> 00:14:58.400
Hey wait a sec! Hey!

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:03.090
At any rate, we should check the places Ayu frequents.

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:05.080
We may find some evidence.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:05.560
Yeah.

00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:09.180
Where is the nearest place you go to frequently?

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:11.870
Umm...

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:14.900
The shop with sweet-flavored things on that corner.

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:15.960
It's a sweets shop.

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:17.530
Wait a sec!

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:19.110
What is it?

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:22.110
Should we bring a schop or something like that?
(TL Note: Schop is Dutch for shovel.)

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:23.230
Huh?

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:25.730
We're going to dig the ground!

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:28.840
Is the Tokugawa Maizoukin what you lost!?
(TL Note: The Tokugawa Maizoukin is the legendary treasure hidden by the Tokugawa family. Many people still search for it.)

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:31.450
Ughuu... I'm joking!

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:39.850
Sweets Shop

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:43.810
Hamburgers

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:49.780
Coffee and karaoke

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:53.240
Taiyaki

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:55.030
Crepe Zakuro

00:15:56.780 --> 00:15:57.620
Well?

00:15:57.840 --> 00:15:59.470
Hmmm... Oh!

00:15:59.550 --> 00:16:00.540
You found it!?

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:04.040
The crepe menu increased its selection in an unknown period of time.

00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:05.080
Go home.

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:07.880
Ughuu... I'm joking.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:11.000
Choose to be either serious or not.

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:13.130
I'm always serious!

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:13.940
Where next?

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:16.920
Hmmm, the cake shop over there.

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:19.470
They're all food shops.

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:20.590
Don't worry about it!

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:21.600
Huh?

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:25.470
It's not here.

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:27.270
That's strange...

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:30.160
I'm sure there was a cake shop.

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:31.030
Let's go.

00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:41.070
After all that, there weren't any clues.

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:44.180
Cheer up.

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:46.030
I'll buy some taiyaki for you.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:48.250
Really!?

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:54.030
Do you want to eat mine too?

00:16:54.170 --> 00:16:55.200
Eh!? It's alright?

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:55.510
Yup.

00:16:57.900 --> 00:16:59.890
Ah, I'm happy.

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:04.180
What the hell. You looked as if the world is about to end.

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:08.080
Girls aren't energetic when they're hungry.

00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:09.650
Is that how it is?

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:10.880
It is like that.

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:13.690
Thanks, Yuuichi-kun.

00:17:14.190 --> 00:17:16.690
I'll do my best to find it tomorrow.

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:17.620
Yeah!

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:19.160
See you! Yuuichi-kun.

00:17:23.250 --> 00:17:26.540
"Girls aren't energetic when they're hungry" ...huh?

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:28.720
Okay!

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:34.170
You're going somewhere?

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:36.330
Yeah, for a while.

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:37.590
Where are you going?

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:38.600
School.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:40.730
That's fishy.

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:41.940
Wh-what is!?

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:43.620
You're hiding something aren't you?

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:45.080
Don't be silly!

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:47.290
First of all, it's something that has nothing to do with you!

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:48.610
I'm leaving.

00:17:50.660 --> 00:17:52.060
What's with that, geez.

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:04.680
I thought you'd be here.

00:18:06.930 --> 00:18:08.410
This is a present.

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:09.230
Gyuudon
(TL Note: Gyuudon is a Yoshinoya beef bowl.)

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:12.150
This isn't really an appreciation for this afternoon, but...
Gyuudon
(TL Note: Gyuudon is a Yoshinoya beef bowl.)

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:12.570
Gyuudon
(TL Note: Gyuudon is a Yoshinoya beef bowl.)

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:13.580
Aren't you hungry?
Gyuudon
(TL Note: Gyuudon is a Yoshinoya beef bowl.)

00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:13.920
Gyuudon
(TL Note: Gyuudon is a Yoshinoya beef bowl.)

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:18.370
Answer me.

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:20.200
Are you hungry or not.

00:18:22.050 --> 00:18:22.830
A bit.

00:18:24.770 --> 00:18:26.530
I see. Then eat.

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:28.300
Mai, do you hate gyuudon?

00:18:29.030 --> 00:18:30.130
I don't hate it.

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:32.090
I see, that's great.

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:34.090
Let's eat it before it gets cold.

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:37.980
What's wrong?

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:39.410
Open the lid.

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:42.100
Here.

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:48.050
Chopsticks, too.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:50.010
You should put your sword down.

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:57.730
Is it delicious?

00:18:58.010 --> 00:18:58.850
It's delicious.

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:00.280
That's great.

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:03.080
You won't be energetic if you're hungry.

00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:05.920
Why?

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:10.830
Why did you come here?

00:19:11.220 --> 00:19:13.520
I wanted to be sure, I guess.

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:14.780
Be sure?

00:19:14.780 --> 00:19:15.730
Yeah.

00:19:15.870 --> 00:19:17.890
That last night's incident was not a dream.

00:19:18.060 --> 00:19:19.660
I just want to be sure with my own eyes.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:21.790
About that monster.

00:19:22.630 --> 00:19:24.710
And about meeting Mai, too.

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:29.170
It's not a dream!

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:33.460
Ah, Hey! Did it come!?

00:19:34.140 --> 00:19:35.540
It's still half-eaten.

00:19:36.460 --> 00:19:37.250
Wait!

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:39.940
You mean defend this gyuudon to the death?

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:48.670
I can't do anything!?

00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:50.770
I can only watch? Damn it!

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:04.320
There wasn't just one!

00:20:33.010 --> 00:20:34.160
Did you kill it?

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:36.690
No.

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:38.370
Does that mean that it ran away?

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:43.360
I see. More importantly, it's good to be safe.

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:48.160
What's wrong?

00:20:52.030 --> 00:20:55.680
Hey, are you saying that gyuudon is more important than me?

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:00.050
No, I wasn't.

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:02.580
Don't lie! What was that pause!? That pause!

00:21:03.810 --> 00:21:04.430
Sorry.

00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:08.550
Hey, you admitted it! You admitted it, huh!?

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:12.590
Ahh well.

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:14.970
I have to clean this up.

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:16.210
Yuuichi.

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:17.050
Hmm.

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:18.850
Thanks.

00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:24.960
What that invisible monster was...

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:27.320
Or why Mai fights...

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:28.920
I don't know...

00:21:30.070 --> 00:21:35.900
But, for now, I was very happy about Mai's words of gratitude.

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:46.080
What can that be?

00:21:47.480 --> 00:21:48.210
Aizawa!

00:21:48.210 --> 00:21:49.530
Hey, what's wrong?

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:51.240
It's not "what's wrong"!

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:53.210
Is it a motorcycle gang?

00:21:53.210 --> 00:21:54.440
It seems to be Kawasumi.

00:21:54.440 --> 00:21:59.070
Last night, it seemed that she ran amuck with a metal pipe.

00:21:59.380 --> 00:21:59.970
Mai!

00:22:02.940 --> 00:22:03.750
Kawasumi-san.

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:06.980
I have something to talk about.

00:22:07.400 --> 00:22:09.170
Please come with us.

00:22:25.270 --> 00:22:30.170
In between the flowing clouds
nagareru kunono aimani

00:22:30.530 --> 00:22:35.910
The crawling blue sky
muzuita aozora ga

00:22:36.530 --> 00:22:41.590
Even causes the familiar town
minareta machinami de sae

00:22:41.850 --> 00:22:47.060
To light up
kagayakasete kureru

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:52.900
Running small back
kaketeku chiisana senaka

00:22:53.160 --> 00:22:58.790
The two at that time were...
anokoro no futariga

00:22:59.200 --> 00:23:04.210
The reason for the spilling pain
koboreru itami no wakewo

00:23:04.470 --> 00:23:09.950
Hidden with innocence
mujyakisa de kakushita

00:23:12.580 --> 00:23:18.320
Time is flowing quietly
tokiwa shizukani nagare

00:23:18.630 --> 00:23:23.950
The gentle winds blow
yasashii kaze ga fuita

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:29.580
Numbed feelings too will
Kajikanda omoimo

00:23:29.830 --> 00:23:35.830
Change to a smile
egao ni kawarukara

